>
>>I've heard that its possible to change the alignment of an altar (instead
>>of yourself).  is it possible?  If so, how?
>
>
>You just offer some corpse on the altar. Be sure not to offer your own
>unicorn, since then you'll change your own alignment, which I actually
>find quite practical when you want to be lawful (easier to get holy water
>by changing all other altars after that to lawful)
>
>By the way, is there any other ways to change alignment apart from the
>unicorn thing and a helm of opposite alignment?
>
>Samuli
Anytime you attempt to convert an altar, it is possible to convert yourself
instead.  It depends on your alignment (if your alignment is low, you'll
be converted instead).  The reason the unicorn thing works is that if 
you've just killed a co-aligned unicorn, your alignment will be very
low.


By the way, a helm of opposite alignment is a VERY good thing to have --
possibly even worth wishing for if you have several wishes.  It will 
let you pray in hell like a chaotic character, and convert all the
alters to lawful to make holy water.
